\[
\begin{pmatrix}
\cos^2(\theta) - \sin^2(\theta) & 2\sin(\theta)\cos(\theta) \\
2\sin(\theta)\cos(\theta) & \sin^2(\theta) - \cos^2(\theta)
\end{pmatrix}
\]
where $\theta$ is the angle the line makes with the x-axis. For the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}$ to be reflected to $\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$, we need to find the correct $\theta$. The slope of 3/4 suggests that $\tan(\theta) = 3/4$, and we can find $\cos(\theta)$ and $\sin(\theta)$ from this. The correct reflection matrix for this transformation is:
\[
\begin{pmatrix}
